-- title:
--   Injectivity of substitution along an isogeny, and descent
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative Noetherian ring, $n$ a natural number, and let $F, F'$ be $n$-dimensional formal group laws over $B$: each is given by an $n$-tuple of power series in $2n$ variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,n$ with vanishing constant term, with the coefficient of each degree-one variable $X_{\mathrm{inl}\,j}$ and $X_{\mathrm{inr}\,j}$ in the $i$-th component equal to $\delta_{ij}$, and satisfying associativity; both are assumed commutative, i.e. interchanging the two blocks of variables fixes each component. Let $\rho = (\rho_i) : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$ have $\rho_i(0) = 0$ for all $i$, and suppose $\rho$ is a homomorphism from $F$ to $F'$, in the sense that $\rho_i(F(x,y)) = F'_i(\rho(x),\rho(y))$ for every $i$. Assume further that there is $N$ with $x_i^N \in (\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ for all $i$, and that $B[\![x]\!]/(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ is finite and projective as a $B$-module. Then: (i) $H \mapsto H(\rho)$ is injective on $B[\![x]\!]$; (ii) the induced substitution $H \mapsto H(\rho(x),\rho(y))$ is injective on power series in the $2n$ variables; and (iii) for every $G \in B[\![x]\!]$ with $G(F(x,y)) - G(x)$ lying in the ideal generated by the $\rho_i(y)$, there exists $H \in B[\![x]\!]$ with $G = H(\rho)$ and $H(0) = G(0)$.
--
--   This is the substitution-injectivity and descent package for a homomorphism of commutative formal group laws whose kernel is a finite flat infinitesimal scheme with nilpotent coordinates: functions on the source that are invariant under translation by the kernel are exactly the functions pulled back from the target. It supplies the construction of quasi-inverses and of factorisations of homomorphisms through a given isogeny, and is used in the treatment of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd uniformisation.
